Z||000000||NEO Cesek Racing||11-07-2001||02:24 PM||||i went ahead and drilled out the rivets on the headlight motor to get at the worn plastic gear inside.  i was under the impression that all i had to do was rotate it to an un-worn side to squeeze some extra life outta the motor.  but alas, i hooked the motor back up and i still have the same problem. when i send the lights up,  the manual control knob just spins. do i need to get a whole new plastic gear? there's only about  4% of the circumference that's worn, so i'm confused.   <BR>one oddity i did notice though, was that the metal pin sticking out where the support bar connects to the motor was also still rotating. which means the plastic gear was rotating. that leads me to believe that it's not the gear after all.  does anyone have any other ideas????<BR>thanks in advance.<P>-AJ<P>------------------<BR>I used to have a handle <BR>on life but it broke.||||reg||5
