Z||000002||Rodrv6||11-07-2001||06:34 PM||||I'm going to assume this is an 84-86 motor.  You say the metal pin that hooks up to the external linkage is rotating and not stopping?  If that's the case, you may have a worn out external link.  The end of the "pin" should have two flat spots in it that mate with a slotted hole in the linkage.  If the link hole has worn to a round shape then the motor may not be able to "stall out" and thereby shut off at the end of the cycle.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
